{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>YHWH [by them they shall live].</b> [It refers] to your word that is mentioned, which he said, 'and he said' — and so by your utterance and your deed there shall be life, and for all, the times in which my spirit lives:" "<b>and you heal me.</b> From the root of יחלמו בניהם (Job 39:4), [meaning] they grow fat with grain, and in the words of our Sages, ZL: times of healing [Rosh HaShanah 28]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The bracketed reading עליהם יחיו and the trailing clause after the colon are textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:54.837253694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}